<article class="env-definition" id="043Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/043Q">Definition <span data-tag="043Q">78.8.1</span>.</a> Let $B \to S$ as in Section <a href="/tag/043A" data-tag="043A">78.3</a>. Let $(G, m)$ be a group algebraic space over $B$. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $B$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An <em>action of $G$ on the algebraic space $X/B$</em> is a morphism $a : G \times _ B X \to X$ over $B$ such that for every scheme $T$ over $B$ the map $a : G(T) \times X(T) \to X(T)$ defines the structure of a $G(T)$-set on $X(T)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Suppose that $X$, $Y$ are algebraic spaces over $B$ each endowed with an action of $G$. An <em>equivariant</em> or more precisely a <em>$G$-equivariant</em> morphism $\psi : X \to Y$ is a morphism of algebraic spaces over $B$ such that for every $T$ over $B$ the map $\psi : X(T) \to Y(T)$ is a morphism of $G(T)$-sets. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>